## 1. What was failing and why

All 7 build errors stem from a single root cause: the compiler is invoked with `-std=c11` (which defines `__STRICT_ANSI__`) and `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`. In glibc's `features.h`, the `__STRICT_ANSI__` definition suppresses `_DEFAULT_SOURCE`, and in this environment the inference from `_POSIX_C_SOURCE` to `__USE_XOPEN2K` (which gates `nftw`, `FTW_PHYS`, `FTW_SL`, `struct ftw`, and `realpath`) is not being triggered. As a result, none of those symbols are declared, producing the cascade of implicit-declaration and undeclared-identifier errors.

The checkpoint test failure ("No such file or directory: 'build/c_cp'") is a direct consequence of the build failure — the binary was never produced.

## 2. What I changed

Added a single feature-test-macro definition as the very first line of the file, before any `#include`:

```c
#define _XOPEN_SOURCE 700
